summary:
  A capture whose time ran out with exit code 0 is called saved, however
  little audio its file holds.

history:
  The verdict asked the wall clock, the exit code and a floor of 10 KB a
  minute. Reported 2026-11-10: asked for 300 s, 302 s gone, the file 7 s old,
  rc=0, 112000 bytes, and the notice read "Recording saved". Measured the same
  day with the real command: a station that sent ten seconds and then held
  the socket silent kept a one-minute capture going for its whole 360 s cap
  and the shell answered rc=0 with 9.98 s in the file. The verdict now asks
  how much audio there is.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecordingEngine.qml

find:
                          && (recWasStopRequested || (recRanFull && recRc === 0 && !recShort))

replace:
                          && (recWasStopRequested || (recRanFull && recRc === 0 && recDone))

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_a_capture_far_short_of_its_length_is_not_called_saved
  and tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_a_short_scheduled_capture_leaves_its_window_to_the_tick.
  Line-neutral.
